{"assets":["/statement-assets/45008a1b0f4a7586969dbc2a5e7fdfd36f57dabe0f25fdb0eac0ee0b580baa77.png","/statement-assets/478c09abf5de389f4c89fbdcce3d9c63c931fefcc8942186fa49d6ef44caeab9.png","/statement-assets/cde9f5ac663d00e046fc9b4b2716ee35386c9e1d867a4031d9e0dbf0ccad3424.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1816","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Ian Visits Mary"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ian and Mary are frogs living on lattice points of the Cartesian coordinate plane, with Ian living on $$$(0,0)$$$ and Mary living on $$$(a,b)$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ian would like to visit Mary by jumping around the Cartesian coordinate plane. Every second, he jumps from his current position $$$(x_p, y_p)$$$ to another lattice point $$$(x_q, y_q)$$$, such that no lattice point other than $$$(x_p, y_p)$$$ and $$$(x_q, y_q)$$$ lies on the segment between point $$$(x_p, y_p)$$$ and point $$$(x_q, y_q)$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As Ian wants to meet Mary as soon as possible, he wants to jump towards point $$$(a,b)$$$ using "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at most $$$2$$$ jumps"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Unfortunately, Ian is not good at maths. Can you help him?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A lattice point is defined as a point with both the $$$x$$$-coordinate and $$$y$$$-coordinate being integers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 500$$$) — the number of test cases. The description of test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first and only line of each test case contains two integers $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ ($$$1\\le a,b\\le 10^9$$$) — the coordinates of the lattice point where Mary lives."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, print an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2$$$) on the first line, denoting the number of jumps Ian uses in order to meet Mary. Note that you do not need to minimize the number of jumps."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"On the $$$i$$$-th line of the next $$$n$$$ lines, print two integers $$$0 \\le x_i,y_i \\le 10^9$$$ separated by a space, denoting Ian's location $$$(x_i,y_i)$$$ after the $$$i$$$-th jump. $$$x_n = a$$$, $$$y_n = b$$$ must hold."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ian's initial location and his locations after each of the $$$n$$$ jumps "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"need not"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" be distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple solutions, output any."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8\n3 4\n4 4\n3 6\n2 2\n1 1\n7 3\n2022 2023\n1000000000 1000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1\n3 4\n2\n3 2\n4 4\n2\n5 3\n3 6\n2\n1 0\n2 2\n1\n1 1\n1\n7 3\n1\n2022 2023\n2\n69420420 469696969\n1000000000 1000000000\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/45008a1b0f4a7586969dbc2a5e7fdfd36f57dabe0f25fdb0eac0ee0b580baa77.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$(0,0) \\to (3,4)$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/478c09abf5de389f4c89fbdcce3d9c63c931fefcc8942186fa49d6ef44caeab9.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$(0,0) \\to (3,2) \\to (4,4)$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/cde9f5ac663d00e046fc9b4b2716ee35386c9e1d867a4031d9e0dbf0ccad3424.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$(0,0) \\to (5,3) \\to (3,6)$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1816A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1816/problem/A"}